/*
# Seamless Explorer

![Seamless Explorer preview](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DavidHiFi/davids-windhawk-mods/main/media/previews/seamless-explorer.png)

35 small File Explorer mods in one. Every one has its own switch at the top of its settings.
Turn a switch off and that part stops. The rest keeps working.

## What is inside

### Look

- **Explorer styler** (`styler`): Dresses File Explorer in the Mocha look with themes and styles you can change.
- **Copy and delete window** (`fileOperations`): A modern look for the copy, move and delete progress window.
- **Icon colours** (`glyphColours`): Gives the blue parts of File Explorer's icons your accent colour or another colour.
- **No focus box** (`hideFocusBorder`): Removes the white box around the selected file.
- **No lines in the folder tree** (`noTreeLines`): Hides the thin lines in the left pane and lets you tighten the spacing.
- **File type icons and names** (`fileTypeProperties`): Pick the icon and the type name for any file ending.
- **Classic menu bar** (`folderMenuBar`): Brings back the menu bar and other classic parts of File Explorer.
- **Tidy folder tree** (`navPaneSpacing`): A thin line between the folder tree and your files, even spacing, and no pin icons.
- **Project folder icons** (`autoFolderIcons`): A folder with its own icon file inside, such as favicon.ico, shows that icon.

### Windows, folders and tabs

- **Tags panel** (`tags`): Adds a Tags panel under the folder tree and a Tags menu to the right-click menu.
- **Home button** (`homeButton`): Adds a Home button next to Refresh in the address bar.
- **Pinned items** (`itemPins`): Keeps the files and folders you choose at the top of their folder.
- **Real folder paths** (`realFolderPaths`): Sidebar shortcuts such as Downloads open the real folder path.
- **Faster folder switching** (`fastNavigation`): Less flicker when you open a folder.
- **Reopen closed tab** (`reopenClosedTab`): Ctrl+Shift+T brings back the last tab you closed.
- **Double-click to go up** (`doubleClickUp`): Double-click empty space to go up one folder.
- **No minimum window size** (`noMinSize`): Lets you make File Explorer windows as small as you like.
- **Shorter window titles** (`noTitleSuffix`): Takes the ending off window titles on the taskbar, for example File Explorer.
- **Status bar details** (`statusMetadata`): Shows size, date, type and length of the selected file in the status bar.
- **Start folder** (`defaultFolder`): Pick the folder a new File Explorer window or tab opens in, or reopen the last one you closed.
- **Keep open tabs** (`tabsSession`): Saves your open File Explorer tabs and opens them again after a restart. Off at first: it works best with Explorer Tab Utility.

### Right-click menu

- **Your own menu items** (`menuCustomItems`): Adds your own commands to the old right-click menu (Show more options).
- **Rename menu items** (`menuCore`): Changes the icons and names of the built-in right-click commands.
- **Hide menu items** (`menuRemoveItems`): Removes the items you do not want from the old right-click menu.
- **Faster right-click menus** (`menuPreload`): Loads the menu parts for the file types you choose ahead of time.
- **Copy contents and hash** (`copyContents`): Adds right-click actions that copy a file's text or its SHA-256 hash.
- **Right-click the whole row** (`rowRightClick`): A right-click anywhere on a file's row opens its menu.

### Files, copying and small fixes

- **Copy queue** (`copyQueue`): Runs copy jobs one after another instead of all at once.
- **Better eject message** (`ejectDialog`): Says which program is using a USB drive when Windows refuses to eject it.
- **F2 twice renames the ending** (`doubleF2`): Press F2 again to select just the file ending.
- **No rename warning** (`noExtensionWarning`): Turns off the warning when you change a file ending.
- **No harmful files question** (`harmfulFilesAccept`): Skips the question 'These files might be harmful' when you drag files.
- **Play key goes to your player** (`mediaKeyFix`): The play key reaches your music player instead of the selected file.
- **Folder tree crash guard** (`treeGuard`): Stops a File Explorer window from closing by itself when the folder tree gets a bad request.
- **Preview downloaded files** (`previewDownloads`): The preview pane shows downloaded PDFs again. The file keeps its downloaded mark, so everything else stays as careful as before.

## Settings

Every part starts with a switch named after it, for example `tags.enabled`. Turning a switch off or on
restarts the mod in File Explorer. Your old settings carry over to the same names under each part.
Each part keeps its saved data in its own folder, so two parts never read each other's files.

Reopen closed tab starts a second, hidden Explorer process to catch the hotkey, as it always did.
It runs only that part.

## When two parts change the same thing

Several parts hook the same Windows functions. They are called one after the other in a fixed order,
the part that was switched on last before this version first, so each part still sees the call.

## Not in here

- Seamless Explorer View (the smooth file lists and icon grids) is its own mod with its own settings window.
- Better file sizes, Never auto-expand tree items and No Store in Open with work in every program,
  so they live in Seamless Look.
- Keyboard shortcut actions live in Seamless Input. Toggle hidden files and Unlock folder in use live
  in Seamless Tools.
- Explorer Search and Peek stay their own mods, because they run in a helper process Windhawk starts.

## Credits

Each part keeps its original licence notice in a comment above its code.

- Explorer styler is Windows 11 File Explorer Styler Plus by DavidHiFi, m417z.
- Copy and delete window is File Operation Styler Plus by DavidHiFi, digART, GPL-3.0.
- Icon colours is [Explorer Glyphs Colorizer](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-glyphs-colorizer) by [crazyboyybs](https://github.com/crazyboyybs), MIT.
- No focus box is [File Explorer Focus Border Remover](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-hide-focus-border) by [NoMorePlz](https://github.com/NoMorePlz), MIT.
- No lines in the folder tree is [Explorer TreeLine Killer](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-treeline-killer) by [Languster](https://github.com/Languster), MIT.
- File type icons and names is [File Type Properties Customization](https://windhawk.net/mods/file-type-properties-customization) by [Momo](https://github.com/FreshP-0325), MIT.
- Classic menu bar is [ExplorerFrame and menubar fixes fork](https://windhawk.net/mods/restore-folder-menubar-25h2) by [Anixx](https://github.com/Anixx), MIT.
- Tags panel is Explorer Tags Plus by DavidHiFi, buedgik, MIT.
- Home button is [File Explorer Address Bar Home Button](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-home-button) by [RobotsNeverDie](https://github.com/RBND), MIT.
- Pinned items is [Explorer Item Pins](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-item-pins) by [CTravkin](https://github.com/CTravkin), MIT.
- Real folder paths is [Explorer real folder paths](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-real-folder-paths) by [Nerdworld](https://github.com/nerdworldDE), MIT.
- Faster folder switching is [Explorer Fast Navigation](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-fast-navigation) by [gilnett](https://github.com/gilnett), GPL-3.0.
- Reopen closed tab is [File Explorer Reopen Closed Tab](https://windhawk.net/mods/file-explorer-reopen-closed-tab) by [Armaninyow](https://github.com/armaninyow), MIT.
- Double-click to go up is [Explorer Double Click Up](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-double-click-up) by [wrldspawn](https://github.com/wrldspawn), MIT.
- No minimum window size is [Explorer No Minimum Window Size](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-no-min-size) by [Anixx](https://github.com/Anixx), MIT.
- Shorter window titles is [Remove Taskbar Window Suffixes](https://windhawk.net/mods/file-explorer-remove-suffixes) by [m417z](https://github.com/m417z), MIT.
- Status bar details is [Explorer Status Bar Metadata](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-status-metadata) by [VitalS](https://github.com/VitalSkib), MIT.
- Your own menu items is [Explorer Context Menu Custom Items](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-context-menu-custom-items) by [Deepak](https://github.com/deepak-raven), MIT.
- Rename menu items is [Explorer Core Context Menu Customizer](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-core-context-menu-customizer) by [akiyorm](https://github.com/akiyorm), MIT.
- Hide menu items is [Remove Context Menu Items](https://windhawk.net/mods/remove-context-menu-items) by [Armaninyow](https://github.com/armaninyow), MIT.
- Faster right-click menus is [Context Menu Preloader](https://windhawk.net/mods/context-menu-preloader) by [Lockframe](https://github.com/Lockframe), MIT.
- Copy contents and hash is [Copy File Contents](https://windhawk.net/mods/copy-file-contents) by [metanoid18](https://github.com/Metanoid18), MIT.
- Right-click the whole row is [Fix Explorer Row Right-Click](https://windhawk.net/mods/fix-explorer-row-right-click) by [iMAboud](https://github.com/iMAboud), MIT.
- Copy queue is [Copy Queue](https://windhawk.net/mods/copy-queue) by [Nerdworld](https://github.com/nerdworldDE), MIT.
- Better eject message is [Better Eject Dialog](https://windhawk.net/mods/better-eject-dialog) by [Ender](https://github.com/EnderDragonEP), GPL-3.0-only.
- F2 twice renames the ending is [Select filename extension on double F2](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-double-f2-rename-extension) by [Marnes](https://github.com/leaumar), MIT.
- No rename warning is [Turn off change file extension warning](https://windhawk.net/mods/extension-change-no-warning) by [m417z](https://github.com/m417z), MIT.
- No harmful files question is [Skip harmful files confirmation](https://windhawk.net/mods/harmful-files-autoaccept) by [Arimodu](https://github.com/Arimodu), MIT.
- Play key goes to your player is [Play-Media-Key fix in Explorer](https://windhawk.net/mods/lm-mediakey-explorer-fix) by [Mark Jansen](https://github.com/learn-more), MIT.
- Folder tree crash guard is Explorer Tree Guard by [DavidHiFi](https://github.com/DavidHiFi).
- Start folder is [Explorer Default Folder](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-default-folder) by [DanRotaru](https://github.com/DanRotaru), MIT.
- Keep open tabs is [Explorer Tabs Session Saver Revamped](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-tabs-session-saver-revamped) by [Peter2oo1](https://github.com/Peter2oo1), MIT.
- Tidy folder tree is [File Explorer navigation pane: thin divider, even padding](https://windhawk.net/mods/explorer-navigation-pane-spacing-fixes) by [NDruce](https://github.com/NDruce), MIT.
- Project folder icons is [Automatic Folder Icons](https://windhawk.net/mods/auto-folder-icons) by [Sanekx Arcs](https://github.com/SanekxArcs), MIT.
- Preview downloaded files is [Enable Preview Pane for Downloaded Files](https://windhawk.net/mods/enable-preview-pane-for-downloads) by [javierpetrucci](https://github.com/javierpetrucci), MIT.

## What's new in 1.1.4

- The side list folds in one smooth glide, the line above This PC and the dot beside it are gone, and
  the separator never turns black. The search box is back. Every path crumb, the ... one too, is one
  tidy rounded box. The bottom of the window stays clean in snapped and narrow windows.

## What's new in 1.1.0

- Five new parts: Start folder, Keep open tabs (off at first), Tidy folder tree, Project folder icons
  and Preview downloaded files.

## What's new in 1.0.0

- First release as its own mod: 30 small Explorer mods, each with a switch. Your settings carry over.
- Remove the separate mods once this one is in.

*/
// ==WindhawkModSettings==
/*
- styler:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Explorer styler: on'
    $description: 'Dresses File Explorer in the Mocha look with themes and styles you can change.'
  - theme: ""
    $name: Theme
    $description: >-
      Themes are collections of styles. For details about the themes below, or for
      information about submitting your own theme, refer to the relevant section
      in the mod details.
    $options:
    - "": None
    - Translucent Explorer11: Translucent Explorer11
    - MicaBar: MicaBar
    - NoCommandBar: NoCommandBar
    - Minimal Explorer11: Minimal Explorer11
    - Tabless: Tabless
    - Matter: Matter
    - WindowGlass: WindowGlass
    - AddressSearchOnly: AddressSearchOnly
    - TintedGlass: TintedGlass
    - LiquidGlass: LiquidGlass
    - MicaTabless: MicaTabless
    - OS26 Liquid Glass: OS26 Liquid Glass
    - OS26 Liquid Glass_variant_Compact: OS26 Liquid Glass (Compact)
    - ZEUSosX_044: ZEUSosX_044
    - Compact Explorer11: Compact Explorer11
    - Float: Float
  - backgroundTranslucentEffect: ""
    $name: Translucent background effect
    $description: >-
      The translucent effect to use for the File Explorer background. For
      additional translucent effects, check out the Translucent Windows mod.
    $options:
    - "": Default for the selected theme
    - default: Windows default
    - acrylicblur: Blur (AccentBlurBehind)
    - acrylic: Acrylic
    - mica: Mica
    - micaAlt: Mica Alt
    - none: None
  - backgroundTranslucentEffectRegion: ""
    $name: Translucent background effect region
    $description: >-
      The region where the translucent background effect is applied.
    $options:
    - "": Entire window
    - explorerFrame: File Explorer frame only
  - styleConstants: [""]
    $name: Style constants
    $description: >-
      Some themes support style constants for customization, such as colors. Refer
      to the theme page for available constants. For technical details, refer to
      the mod description.
  - controlStyles:
    - - target: ""
        $name: Target
      - styles: [""]
        $name: Styles
    $name: Control styles
  - themeResourceVariables: [""]
    $name: Resource variables
    $description: >-
      Use "Key=Value" to override an existing resource with a new value.

      Use "Key@Dark=Value" or "Key@Light=Value" to define theme-aware resources
      that can be referenced with {ThemeResource Key} in styles.

      The ":=" syntax can be used to set a XAML value. For details, refer to the
      mod description.
  - explorerFrameContainerHeight: 0
    $name: Explorer frame container height
    $description: >-
      The height of the explorer frame container which includes the tabs, the
      address bar, and the command bar, set to zero to use the default height.
  - statusBarDock: true
    $name: Status bar dock
    $description: >-
      Draws the status bar at the bottom of the window (item count, selection
      size, view buttons) on a rounded Catppuccin Mocha dock, with hover and
      current view rings on the view buttons.
  - navPaneDock: true
    $name: Folder list dock
    $description: >-
      Puts the folder list on the left on its own rounded dock that ends under
      the last folder, with a button at its top left that folds the list to a
      narrow strip and back.
  - navPaneDockAnimation: true
    $name: Folder list fold animation
    $description: >-
      The folder list slides smoothly when you fold or unfold it. Off, it snaps
      straight to its new width. Also off when Windows animation effects are
      off.
  - navPaneDockAnimationSpeed: global
    $name: Fold animation speed
    $description: How quick the fold slide plays.
    $options:
    - global: Same as all my mods
    - veryQuick: Very quick
    - quick: Quick
    - normal: Normal
    - relaxed: Relaxed
    - slow: Slow
  - titleUptime: true
    $name: Uptime after the title
    $description: >-
      Shows how long the window has been open after the folder name, the same
      way Seamless Title Bars shows it on every other window. Look and units
      follow that mod's uptime settings.
  - xamlDiagnosticsHandling: alert
    $name: XAML diagnostics consumer handling
    $description: >-
      How to handle other programs (e.g. ExplorerBlurMica) that try to use XAML
      diagnostics. There can only be one consumer at a time. Block will prevent
      other programs from using it, which might break them. Allow will let them
      use it, which might break this mod.
    $options:
    - alert: Alert (prompt before blocking)
    - block: Block other consumers
    - allow: Allow other consumers
  $name: Explorer styler
- fileOperations:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Copy and delete window: on'
    $description: 'A modern look for the copy, move and delete progress window.'
  - renderer: gpu
    $name: Renderer
    $description: 'GPU draws through the compositor and only repaints when values change. Legacy uses the original GDI+ painting (Suggested: GPU)'
    $options:
    - gpu: GPU (DirectComposition)
    - gdi: Legacy (GDI+)

  - showCurrentFileProgressBar: true
    $name: Show current-file progress bar
    $description: 'Turn on to show progress for the file currently being copied or moved (Suggested: on)'

  - hideSmallControlButtons: false
    $name: Hide small control buttons
    $description: 'Turn on to hide the small Pause / Resume and Cancel controls in the upper-right corner. The progress circle and bottom Cancel button remain available (Suggested: off)'

  - hideTitleBarPercentage: false
    $name: Hide title-bar percentage
    $description: 'Turn on to hide the normal progress percentage from the visible window title bar (Suggested: off)'


  - customization:
    - enabled: false
      $name: Enable customization
      $description: 'Turn on to use themes and custom style settings (Suggested: off)'
    - preset: blueDark
      $name: Theme
      $description: Change color theme.
      $options:
      - blueDark: Blue Dark
      - graphite: Graphite
      - midnight: Midnight
      - warmDark: Warm Dark
      - light: Light
      - system: Windows / System
      - glass: Frosted Glass

    - glassEffect: acrylic
      $name: Frosted Glass style
      $description: Choose the glass effect used by the Frosted Glass theme.
      $options:
      - acrylic: Windows Acrylic
      - blur: Custom Blur
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass}

    - glassTint: "#000000"
      $name: Blur tint
      $description: 'Tint color used by Custom Blur. Color as #RRGGBB (Suggested: #000000)'
      #! $format: colorRgb
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass, glassEffect: blur}

    - glassTintStrength: 0
      $name: Glass opacity
      $description: 'Higher values make Custom Blur less transparent while keeping the selected tint color. 0 to 100 (Suggested: 0)'
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass, glassEffect: blur}

    - footerStyle: glass
      $name: Footer
      $description: Frosted Glass footer is available only when the Frosted Glass theme is selected.
      $options:
      - glass: Frosted Glass
      - solid: Solid
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass}
    - footerColorPreset: theme
      $name: Solid footer color preset
      $description: Used when Frosted Glass is selected with a Solid footer.
      $options:
      - theme: Theme default
      - blueDark: Blue Dark
      - graphite: Graphite
      - midnight: Midnight
      - warmDark: Warm Dark
      - light: Light
      - system: Windows / System
      - custom: Custom
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass, footerStyle: solid}
    - footerColor: ""
      $name: Solid footer custom color
      $description: 'Used only when Solid footer color preset is Custom. Color as #RRGGBB, for example #1C3346'
      #! $showIf: {preset: glass, footerStyle: solid, footerColorPreset: custom}
    - colors:
      - backgroundOverride: ""
        $name: Background
      - accentOverride: ""
        $name: Accent
        $description: Circle, progress bar, graph, and links.
      - primaryTextOverride: ""
        $name: Main text
        $description: Large numbers and values.
      - secondaryTextOverride: ""
        $name: Secondary text
        $description: Labels and smaller text.
      - inactiveOverride: ""
        $name: Track / inactive
        $description: Circle track and progress track.
      $name: Colors
      $description: "Leave blank to use the theme color. Enter a hex color such as #2D8BE0."
    - style:
      - circleThickness: 7
        $name: Circle thickness
        $description: 'Width of the progress circle. 1 to 30 (Suggested: 7)'
      - progressThickness: 8
        $name: Progress bar thickness
        $description: 'Height of the progress bar. 2 to 20 (Suggested: 8)'
      $name: Progress style
    - text:
      - fontPreset: default
        $name: Font
        $description: Choose one font for the whole window.
        $options:
        - default: Windows default
        - segoeUI: Segoe UI
        - segoeUIVariable: Segoe UI Variable
        - arial: Arial
        - calibri: Calibri
        - tahoma: Tahoma
        - verdana: Verdana
        - trebuchetMS: Trebuchet MS
        - georgia: Georgia
        - timesNewRoman: Times New Roman
        - consolas: Consolas
      - customFont: ""
        $name: Custom font
        $description: Optional. An installed font name to use instead of the selection above
      - bodySize: 11
        $name: Details text size
        $description: 'Source and destination, items, speed, time, Complete, and footer text. 8 to 24 (Suggested: 11)'
      - summarySize: 23
        $name: Summary text size
        $description: 'The large transferred / total line, for example 1.2 GB / 4.0 GB. 14 to 48 (Suggested: 23)'
      - percentSize: 26
        $name: Circle percentage size
        $description: 'The percentage number inside the progress circle. 14 to 56 (Suggested: 26)'
      $name: Text
    $name: Customization
  $name: Copy and delete window
- glyphColours:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Icon colours: on'
    $description: 'Gives the blue parts of File Explorer''s icons your accent colour or another colour.'
  - colorMode: accent
    $name: Color source
    $description: Choose the Windows accent indicator shade, a neutral glyph stroke color, or a custom RGB color.
    $options:
    - accent: Windows accent indicator
    - neutral: Match neutral glyph color
    - custom: Custom color
  - customColor: "#FF8C00"
    $name: Custom color
    $description: RGB hex color, such as #FF8C00. Used when Color source is Custom color.
  $name: Icon colours
- hideFocusBorder:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'No focus box: on'
    $description: 'Removes the white box around the selected file.'
  $name: No focus box
- noTreeLines:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'No lines in the folder tree: on'
    $description: 'Hides the thin lines in the left pane and lets you tighten the spacing.'
  - hideSystemSeparatorLines: true
    $name: Fully hide system separator lines
    $description: Hides the default separator line used by the lower special container.
  - removeUpperGap: true
    $name: Remove upper empty space
    $description: Removes the gap between the Home/Gallery block (when visible) and the pinned items list. Enabled = compact mode, disabled = standard spacing.
  - removeLowerGap: true
    $name: Remove lower empty space
    $description: Removes the gap between the pinned items list and This PC. Enabled = compact mode, disabled = standard spacing.
  $name: No lines in the folder tree
- fileTypeProperties:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'File type icons and names: on'
    $description: 'Pick the icon and the type name for any file ending.'
  - enableIcons: true
    $name: Customize icons
    $description: Enable icon overrides. Changing this option reloads the mod.
  - enableDescriptions: true
    $name: Customize type descriptions
    $description: Enable description overrides in supported Shell views and menus. Changing this option reloads the mod.
  - properties:
    - - extensions: ""
        $name: Extensions
        $description: Comma-separated file extensions, including the dot. For example, .txt,.log
      - icon: ""
        $name: Icon
        $description: Absolute icon path, optionally followed by an index. Leave empty to keep the preset or system icon.
      - description: ""
        $name: Description
        $description: Text or @module,-resourceID. Resource paths must be absolute. Leave empty to keep the preset or system description.
    $name: File type properties
    $description: These values override the INI per property. Fill in the first entry; a completely empty entry ends the list.
  - useIni: false
    $name: Load INI preset
    $description: Read the INI first, then apply the list above as per-property overrides. No files are modified.
  - iniPath: "%USERPROFILE%\\FileTypeProperties\\properties.ini"
    $name: INI preset path
    $description: Absolute path, used only when Load INI preset is enabled. Re-enable the mod after editing the file, or save a changed mod setting.
  - refreshExplorer: false
    $name: Refresh Explorer when mappings change
    $description: Refresh cached icons and type names after saving changed mappings, including the first or last rule. May redraw windows and reload thumbnails. Keeps the mod loaded without hooks when no rules are configured. Usually leave off.
  $name: File type icons and names
- folderMenuBar:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Classic menu bar: on'
    $description: 'Brings back the menu bar and other classic parts of File Explorer.'
  - DisplayMenuBar: true
    $name: Display menu bar
    $description: Show the classic menu bar in Explorer windows.
  - ControlPanelColorFix: true
    $name: Control Panel color fix
    $description: Fix white header and sidebar in Control Panel when using dark themes.
  $name: Classic menu bar
- navPaneSpacing:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Tidy folder tree: on'
    $description: 'A thin line between the folder tree and your files, even spacing, and no pin icons.'
  - navPaneDivider: true
    $name: Thin divider between the navigation pane and the files area
    $description: >-
      Replaces the strip between the navigation pane and the files area with a
      line of 1 pixel, of the same color as the line below the command bar. The
      navigation pane can still be resized by dragging the divider.
  - navPaneDividerColor: ""
    $name: Color of the thin divider
    $description: >-
      In the #RRGGBB format, for example #3A3A3A. Leave empty to use a color
      which matches the light or the dark theme. Used if the thin divider is
      turned on.
  - navPanePadding: 1
    $name: Padding of the navigation pane
    $description: >-
      The gap to the left and to the right of the items of the navigation pane,
      the same on both sides, from 0 to 32. The stock gaps are 2 on the left and
      1 on the right. Set to -1 to keep the stock gaps.
  - navPanePaddingVertical: 6
    $name: Vertical padding of the navigation pane
    $description: >-
      The space above and below the contents of the navigation pane, up to 64.
      Set to 0 to keep the stock look.
  - navPinIconsHide: true
    $name: Hide the pin icons
    $description: >-
      Hides the pin icons which are shown to the right of the pinned folders.
  - navPinIconOpacity: 0
    $name: Opacity of the pin icons
    $description: >-
      In percent, from 1 to 99. Used if the pin icons aren't hidden. Set to 0 to
      keep the stock look of the pin icons.
  - navSeparatorInset: 0
    $name: Side gaps of the separators
    $description: >-
      Added to the gaps on the left and on the right of the horizontal lines
      which separate the groups of the navigation pane, from -64 to 64. The
      stock gap is 8. A negative value makes the lines longer: with -8, they go
      from edge to edge of the navigation pane. A positive value makes them
      shorter. Set to 0 to keep the stock gaps.
  - navArrowOffset: -1
    $name: Vertical offset of the expand arrows
    $description: >-
      In pixels, from -8 to 8. A negative value moves the arrows up. Applies to
      all tree views of the process, and takes effect when the tree is redrawn.
      Set to 0 to keep the stock position.
  $name: Tidy folder tree
- autoFolderIcons:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Project folder icons: on'
    $description: 'A folder with its own icon file inside, such as favicon.ico, shows that icon.'
  - useFavicon: true
    $name: Use favicon.ico
    $description: >-
      Also use favicon.ico as a folder icon when there is no folder.ico. Turn
      this off if folders of web projects get icons you don't want.
  $name: Project folder icons
- tags:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Tags panel: on'
    $description: 'Adds a Tags panel under the folder tree and a Tags menu to the right-click menu.'
  - tags:
    - - name: Important
        $name: Name
      - color: "#E81123"
        $name: Color
        $description: 'Color as #RRGGBB, for example #E81123'
    $name: Tags
    $description: Each tag has a name and a color.
  - folder: ""
    $name: Tags folder
    $description: >-
      Where the shortcut folders go, one per tag. Empty uses %USERPROFILE%\Tags.

      Changing this rebuilds the shortcuts under the new folder and leaves the
      old one behind. Avoid synced folders (OneDrive, Dropbox, network shares):
      a shortcut missing mid-sync looks like a tag you removed. The whole tree
      under this folder is watched, so keep it out of busy folders.
  - maxRows: 8
    $name: Visible rows
    $description: 'With more tags than this, the panel scrolls with the mouse wheel. 1 to 40 (Suggested: 8)'
  - foldAnimation: true
    $name: Animate folding
    $description: >-
      Slide and fade the panel away when the folder list folds, and back when it
      opens. Follows the global motion speed, and stays still when Windows
      animations are off.
  $name: Tags panel
- homeButton:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Home button: on'
    $description: 'Adds a Home button next to Refresh in the address bar.'
  - targetLocation: "shell:MyComputerFolder"
    $name: Target Location
    $description: >-
      The Shell location, CLSID, or folder path to open in the active tab when the
      Home button is clicked. Defaults to "shell:MyComputerFolder"
      (::{20D04FE0-3AEA-1069-A2D8-08002B30309D}).
  - placement: after
    $name: Button Placement
    $description: >-
      Place the Home button immediately before or after the Refresh button in the
      address bar.
    $options:
      - before: Before Refresh button
      - after: After Refresh button
  - iconGlyph: home
    $name: Icon Glyph
    $description: >-
      Select the Segoe Fluent Icons glyph displayed on the button.
    $options:
      - home: Home (E80F)
      - computer: Computer / This PC (E770)
  - tooltip: "This PC"
    $name: Tooltip Text
    $description: >-
      The tooltip shown when hovering over the Home button. Defaults to "This PC".
  $name: Home button
- itemPins:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Pinned items: on'
    $description: 'Keeps the files and folders you choose at the top of their folder.'
  - display:
      - contextMenu: true
        $name: Context menu command
      - commandBar: true
        $name: Command bar button
      - pinIndicator: true
        $name: Pinned item indicator
    $name: Show elements
  $name: Pinned items
- realFolderPaths:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Real folder paths: on'
    $description: 'Sidebar shortcuts such as Downloads open the real folder path.'
  $name: Real folder paths
- fastNavigation:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Faster folder switching: on'
    $description: 'Less flicker when you open a folder.'
  - navigationPaint: true
    $name: Defer immediate navigation paints
    $description: Defer immediate activation and layout paints while Explorer switches views. Native loading and redraw
      protection remain active.
  - classicRibbon: true
    $name: Defer classic ribbon updates
    $description: Delay classic ribbon refreshes during navigation.
  - xamlCommandBar: true
    $name: Defer XAML command bar updates
    $description: Delay modern command bar refreshes during navigation. Navigation bar updates have a separate switch.
  - navigationBar: true
    $name: Defer navigation bar updates
    $description: Delay navigation state updates in both the classic and modern navigation bars.
  - groupedFolderBatching: true
    $name: Accelerate grouped folder batching
    $description: Shorten Explorer's internal grouping timer interval on grouped views while preserving standard
      non-grouped behavior.
  - safetyCeilingMs: 2000
    $name: Safety fallback ceiling (ms)
    $description: Maximum time in milliseconds before forcing pending UI updates to flush if navigation stalls or on slow network drives.
  $name: Faster folder switching
- reopenClosedTab:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Reopen closed tab: on'
    $description: 'Ctrl+Shift+T brings back the last tab you closed.'
  $name: Reopen closed tab
- doubleClickUp:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Double-click to go up: on'
    $description: 'Double-click empty space to go up one folder.'
  $name: Double-click to go up
- noMinSize:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'No minimum window size: on'
    $description: 'Lets you make File Explorer windows as small as you like.'
  $name: No minimum window size
- noTitleSuffix:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Shorter window titles: on'
    $description: 'Takes the ending off window titles on the taskbar, for example File Explorer.'
  - suffixRemovalMode: fileExplorerOnly
    $name: Suffix removal mode
    $options:
    - off: Off
    - fileExplorerOnly: File Explorer only
    - universal: Universal
    $description: >-
      Controls how suffixes are removed from taskbar titles. "File Explorer only"
      only removes File Explorer suffixes. "Universal" removes the suffix from any
      title (e.g., "Document - Editor" becomes "Document").
  - suffixRules:
    - - processIdentifier: ""
        $name: Process (name, path, or App ID)
        $description: >-
          Can be a process name (explorer.exe), full path
          (C:\Windows\explorer.exe), or App ID
          (Microsoft.WindowsCalculator_8wekyb3d8bbwe!App). Leave empty to match
          all processes.
      - search: ""
        $name: Search pattern (regex)
        $description: >-
          Regular expression pattern to search for in window titles. Example: " -
          Notepad$" to match " - Notepad" at the end of the title.
      - replace: ""
        $name: Replace with
        $description: >-
          Replacement text. Can use regex capture groups ($1, $2, etc.). Leave
          empty to remove the matched text.
    $name: Custom title modification rules
    $description: >-
      Define regex-based search and replace rules for window titles. Each rule
      specifies a process and a regex pattern. Multiple rules can match the same
      window, and all matching patterns are applied in order.
  $name: Shorter window titles
- statusMetadata:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Status bar details: on'
    $description: 'Shows size, date, type and length of the selected file in the status bar.'
  - allowNetworkDrives: false
    $name: Enable metadata on network drives (UNC paths)
    $description: >
      WARNING: May cause Explorer to freeze for several seconds if the network
      is slow or unavailable. The metadata lookup is synchronous on the UI thread.
      Only enable this if you are on a fast, reliable local network.

  - allowRemovableDrives: true
    $name: Enable metadata on removable drives (USB, SD cards)
    $description: >
      Metadata lookup on slow removable media (e.g. old USB drives) may cause
      a brief UI stutter. Fast USB 3.x drives are generally fine.

  - cacheEvictCount: 10
    $name: Cache eviction count
    $description: >
      When the cache reaches 1000 entries, this many of the oldest entries
      are removed. Range: 1-50. Lower values preserve more history;
      higher values free more memory at once.
  $name: Status bar details
- defaultFolder:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Start folder: on'
    $description: 'Pick the folder a new File Explorer window or tab opens in, or reopen the last one you closed.'
  - defaultFolder: ""
    $name: Default folder
    $description: >-
      Folder opened in new Explorer windows and tabs. Accepts normal paths,
      environment variables (%USERPROFILE%\Downloads), paths relative to your
      user folder (~\Downloads or just Downloads) and shell locations
      (shell:Downloads). Leave empty to keep Explorer's default behavior.
  - applyTo: both
    $name: Apply to
    $description: >-
      Which new Explorer instances are redirected, to the default folder or to
      the last closed folder.
    $options:
    - both: Both (new window and new tab)
    - window: New window
    - tab: New tab
  - reopenLastClosed: false
    $name: Reopen last closed folder (ignores Default folder)
    $description: >-
      Open the folder of the most recently closed Explorer window or tab instead
      of the Default folder. The Default folder is only used until a folder has
      been closed, or if the last closed folder no longer exists.
  $name: Start folder
- tabsSession:
  - enabled: false
    $name: 'Keep open tabs: on'
    $description: 'Saves your open File Explorer tabs and opens them again after a restart. Off at first: it works best with Explorer Tab Utility.'
  - reuseInitialTab: true
    $name: Reuse initial tab on restore
    $description: Navigate the initial Home / This PC tab in-place to the first saved tab instead of leaving an extra default tab on the left.
  - lockSidebarScroll: true
    $name: Prevent sidebar auto-scroll to bottom on restore
    $description: Lock the Navigation Pane scroll position to the top while tabs are being restored.
  $name: Keep open tabs
- menuCustomItems:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Your own menu items: on'
    $description: 'Adds your own commands to the old right-click menu (Show more options).'
  - items:
    - - label: ""
        $name: Label
        $description: The text to show in the context menu.
      - command: ""
        $name: Command
        $description: The command line to execute. Use %1 for the selected file path.
      - extensions: ""
        $name: File Extensions (Optional)
        $description: Comma-separated list of extensions (e.g., .mp4, .mkv). Leave empty for all files.
      - allowFolders: true
        $name: Show on Folders
        $description: Toggle whether this option should appear when right-clicking folders or folder backgrounds.
  $name: Your own menu items
- menuCore:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Rename menu items: on'
    $description: 'Changes the icons and names of the built-in right-click commands.'
  - open:
    - enabled: true
      $name: Enabled
    - iconPath: "imageres.dll,-185"
      $name: Icon path or DLL index
      $description: Default is imageres.dll,-185. Leave empty for no icon, or enter a .ico path or DLL index (e.g. shell32.dll,44).
    - customText: ""
      $name: Custom label
      $description: Leave empty for the default system name. Supports %file% (truncated after 30 characters).
    $name: Open
  - runAs:
    - enabled: true
      $name: Enabled
    - iconPath: ""
      $name: Icon path or DLL index
      $description: Leave empty to keep the default Windows UAC shield, or enter a .ico path or DLL index (e.g. shell32.dll,44).
    - customText: ""
      $name: Custom label
      $description: Leave empty for the default system name. Supports %file% (truncated after 30 characters).
    $name: Run as administrator
  - delete:
    - enabled: true
      $name: Enabled
    - iconPath: "imageres.dll,-54"
      $name: Icon path or DLL index
      $description: Default is Full Recycle Bin (imageres.dll,-54). Leave empty for no icon, or enter a .ico path or DLL index (e.g. shell32.dll,44).
    - customText: ""
      $name: Custom label
      $description: Leave empty for the default system name. Supports %file% (truncated after 30 characters).
    $name: Delete
  - rename:
    - enabled: true
      $name: Enabled
    - iconPath: "shell32.dll,-16763"
      $name: Icon path or DLL index
      $description: Default is Clipboard (shell32.dll,-16763). Leave empty for no icon, or enter a .ico path or DLL index (e.g. shell32.dll,44).
    - customText: "Rename: '%file%'"
      $name: Custom label
      $description: "Default is Rename: '%file%'. Leave empty for the default system name. Supports %file% (truncated after 30 characters)."
    $name: Rename
  - properties:
    - enabled: true
      $name: Enabled
    - iconPath: "imageres.dll,-114"
      $name: Icon path or DLL index
      $description: Default is imageres.dll,-114. Leave empty for no icon, or enter a .ico path or DLL index (e.g. shell32.dll,44).
    - customText: ""
      $name: Custom label
      $description: Leave empty for the default system name. Supports %file% (truncated after 30 characters).
    $name: Properties
  $name: Rename menu items
- menuRemoveItems:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Hide menu items: on'
    $description: 'Removes the items you do not want from the old right-click menu.'

  - bloatwareItems:
    - removeOneDrive: true
      $name: Move to OneDrive
    - removeCopilot: true
      $name: Ask Copilot
    - removeDefender: true
      $name: Scan with Microsoft Defender...
    - removeDesigner: true
      $name: Create with Designer
    - removeClipchamp: true
      $name: Edit with Clipchamp
    - removeMicrosoft365Copilot: true
      $name: Ask Microsoft 365 Copilot
    $name: Bloatware Items
    $description: Enabled by default

  - basicItems:
    - removeOpen: false
      $name: Open
    - removeOpenWith: false
      $name: Open with
    - removeCut: false
      $name: Cut
    - removeCopy: false
      $name: Copy
    - removeCreateShortcut: false
      $name: Create shortcut
    - removeDelete: false
      $name: Delete
    - removeRename: false
      $name: Rename
    - removeSendTo: false
      $name: Send to
    - removeOpenInNewTab: false
      $name: Open in new tab
    - removeOpenInNewWindow: false
      $name: Open in new window
    - removeEdit: false
      $name: Edit
    - removePlay: false
      $name: Play
    - removePreview: false
      $name: Preview
    - removePrint: false
      $name: Print
    - removeShare: false
      $name: Share
    - removeRefresh: false
      $name: Refresh
    - removeCopyAsPath: false
      $name: Copy as path
    - removeCustomizeFolder: false
      $name: Customize this folder...
    - removeFavorites: false
      $name: Add to Favorites
    - removePinToQuickAccess: false
      $name: Pin to Quick access
    - removePinToStart: false
      $name: Pin to Start
    - removeCast: false
      $name: Cast to Device
    - removeGiveAccess: false
      $name: Give access to
    - removeRestoreVersions: false
      $name: Restore previous versions
    - removeIncludeInLibrary: false
      $name: Include in library
    - removeRotate: false
      $name: Rotate options
      $description: The "Rotate right" and "Rotate left" items
    - removeDisplaySettings: false
      $name: Display settings
      $description: Desktop menu item
    - removePersonalize: false
      $name: Personalize
      $description: Desktop menu item
    - removeSetAsDesktopBackground: false
      $name: Set as desktop background
    - removeView: false
      $name: View
    - removeSortBy: false
      $name: Sort by
    - removeGroupBy: false
      $name: Group by
    - removeNew: false
      $name: New
    - removeProperties: false
      $name: Properties
    - removePaste: false
      $name: Paste
      $description: Only when greyed-out
    - removeExtractAll: false
      $name: Extract All...
    $name: Basic Items
    $description: Disabled by default

  - appSpecificItems:
    - removeSendWithQuickShare: false
      $name: Send with Quick Share
    - removeVLCPlaylist: false
      $name: Add to VLC media player's Playlist
    - removeVLCPlay: false
      $name: Play with VLC media player
    - removeAddToMediaPlayerQueue: false
      $name: Add to Media Player play queue
    - removePlayWithMediaPlayer: false
      $name: Play with Media Player
    - removeEditInNotepad: false
      $name: Edit in Notepad
      $description: Enable extension filtering below to show this only for relevant file types
    - removeEditInNotepadPlusPlus: false
      $name: Edit with Notepad++
      $description: Enable extension filtering below to show this only for relevant file types
    - removeEditWithPhotos: false
      $name: Edit with Photos
    - removeEditWithPaint: false
      $name: Edit with Paint
    - removeNvidiaApp: false
      $name: NVIDIA App
      $description: Desktop menu item
    - removeOpenInTerminal: false
      $name: Open in Terminal
    - removeAlwaysKeepOnThisDevice: false
      $name: Always keep on this device
      $description: OneDrive menu item
    - removeFreeUpSpace: false
      $name: Free up space
      $description: OneDrive menu item
    - removeWinRAR: false
      $name: WinRAR
      $description: Enable extension filtering below to show this only for relevant file types
    $name: App-specific Items
    $description: Disabled by default

  - customItems:
    - ""
    $name: Custom items to remove
    $description: >-
      Basic Usage (Exact Match): Enter exact menu item names.

      Wildcard Usage (Prefix Match): Add * at the end for prefix matching (e.g., "Open*" removes all items starting with "Open")

  - modifierKeyOverride:
    - enableModifierOverride: false
      $name: Enable modifier key override
      $description: >-
        When enabled, holding Ctrl or Alt while right-clicking temporarily bypasses the mod and shows all original context menu items.
    - overrideKey: ctrl
      $name: Override key
      $description: Which modifier key to hold while right-clicking to bypass filtering
      $options:
      - ctrl: Ctrl
      - alt: Alt
      - both: Both
    $name: Modifier Key Override
    $description: Hold a modifier key while right-clicking to see all original menu items

  - extensionFiltering:
    - enableExtensionFiltering: false
      $name: Enable Notepad extension filtering
      $description: >-
        When enabled, "Edit in Notepad" and "Edit with Notepad++" will ONLY appear for files whose extensions are in the Notepad whitelist below. They are hidden for all other file types. (Note: Requires "Edit in Notepad" or "Edit with Notepad++" menu items to be enabled.)
    - notepadExtensions:
      - ".txt"
      - ".log"
      - ".json"
      - ".xml"
      - ".html"
      - ".css"
      - ".js"
      - ".ts"
      - ".md"
      - ".csv"
      - ".sql"
      - ".yaml"
      - ".yml"
      - ".py"
      - ".java"
      - ".c"
      - ".cpp"
      - ".cs"
      $name: Extensions for Notepad/Notepad++
      $description: Use lowercase with dot (e.g., .txt)
    - enableWinRARFiltering: false
      $name: Enable WinRAR extension filtering
      $description: >-
        When enabled, the WinRAR menu item will ONLY appear for files whose extensions are in the WinRAR whitelist below. It is hidden for all other file types. (Note: Requires "WinRAR" menu item to be enabled.)
    - winrarExtensions:
      - ".zip"
      - ".rar"
      - ".7z"
      - ".iso"
      - ".tar"
      - ".gz"
      - ".tgz"
      - ".bz2"
      - ".xz"
      - ".zst"
      - ".cab"
      $name: Extensions for WinRAR
      $description: Use lowercase with dot (e.g., .zip)
    $name: Extension Filtering
    $description: >-
      On Windows 11, Notepad and WinRAR items can appear even when right-clicking unrelated files. Use the Extension Filtering to show each only for relevant file types.
  $name: Hide menu items
- menuPreload:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Faster right-click menus: on'
    $description: 'Loads the menu parts for the file types you choose ahead of time.'
  - StartupDelay: 5
    $name: Startup Delay (Seconds)
    $description: Wait time before locking handlers.
  - CustomExtensions: "pdf; mp4; mkv; docx; obj; html"
    $name: Custom Extensions
    $description: Extensions to preload and pin. Separate with each ';'.
  - EnableDebug: false
    $name: Enable Debug Logging and RAM usage report.
  $name: Faster right-click menus
- copyContents:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Copy contents and hash: on'
    $description: 'Adds right-click actions that copy a file''s text or its SHA-256 hash.'
  - maxSize: 8
    $name: Largest file to copy
    $description: Files bigger than this are skipped. If nothing is copied, an oversized local file up to 32 MB may be offered in Notepad if its prefix looks like text. The unit is the setting below it, and 64 MB is the most this can ever be. A megabyte here is 1,048,576 bytes, the same as Windows shows in the file listing. One copy holds at most 32 MB of text in all, so no single file is copied beyond that, whatever this is set to.
  - maxSizeUnit: mb
    $name: Size unit
    $description: Megabytes or kilobytes. Whole numbers only; for one and a half megabytes, pick kilobytes and enter 1536.
    $options:
    - mb: Megabytes
    - kb: Kilobytes
  - copyContents: true
    $name: Show "Copy contents"
    $description: Adds the entry that puts the file's text on the clipboard.
  - copyHash: true
    $name: Show "Copy SHA-256"
    $description: Adds the entry that puts the file's SHA-256 hash on the clipboard.
  - offerEditor: true
    $name: Offer to open a file that cannot be copied
    $description: When no file contents can be read, report the reason. Offer Notepad only for an oversized local file up to 32 MB whose prefix looks like text. This does not control warnings for a failed clipboard write or a hash operation with no result.
  - hideWhenUncopyable: true
    $name: Hide "Copy contents" when nothing can be copied
    $description: When every selected file is binary or over the size limit, the entry is left out of the menu instead of being offered and then refusing. The first few KiB of each file are read to decide, except files that are offline, stored online only, or on a network share or a mapped network drive, which are not read.
  - separateEntries: false
    $name: Put each file on the clipboard as its own item
    $description: When several files are copied, each one goes on the clipboard in turn instead of being joined into one text. Windows clipboard history (Win+V) then lists them separately and you can paste any of them. Ctrl+V pastes only the last file. Needs clipboard history turned on, otherwise only the last file is reachable, and history keeps 25 entries of about 4 MB each, so a file over that limit is written last and can only be pasted with Ctrl+V.
  - separateGapMs: 250
    $name: Wait between separate items, in milliseconds
    $description: Windows clipboard history ignores copies that arrive too close together, so the files are written with a short wait between them. Raise this if some files still go missing from the history, lower it if the copy feels slow. 0 turns the wait off.
  - askHashMB: 256
    $name: Ask before hashing files bigger than this in all, in MB
    $description: Hashing reads every byte and the File Explorer window waits until it is done. Above this much in total the mod asks first, using the file sizes it could read. 0 asks for every file whose size can be read.
  - hotkeys: true
    $name: Keyboard shortcuts
    $description: Turn the two shortcuts on. They only act in a File Explorer window with files selected, and never while you type in a rename box, the address bar or the search box.
  - contentsModifiers: ctrl_shift
    $name: Modifiers for the contents shortcut
    $description: Ctrl+Shift is the default. Combinations with Alt are not offered, because File Explorer then waits for the rest of a menu shortcut and gets stuck in that state.
    $options:
    - ctrl_shift: Ctrl+Shift
    - win_shift: Win+Shift
  - contentsKey: T
    $name: Key for the contents shortcut
    $description: A letter, a digit, or F1 to F24
  - hashModifiers: ctrl_shift
    $name: Modifiers for the hash shortcut
    $description: Ctrl+Shift is the default. Combinations with Alt are not offered, because File Explorer then waits for the rest of a menu shortcut and gets stuck in that state.
    $options:
    - ctrl_shift: Ctrl+Shift
    - win_shift: Win+Shift
  - hashKey: H
    $name: Key for the hash shortcut
    $description: A letter, a digit, or F1 to F24
  $name: Copy contents and hash
- rowRightClick:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Right-click the whole row: on'
    $description: 'A right-click anywhere on a file''s row opens its menu.'
  $name: Right-click the whole row
- copyQueue:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Copy queue: on'
    $description: 'Runs copy jobs one after another instead of all at once.'
  $name: Copy queue
- ejectDialog:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Better eject message: on'
    $description: 'Says which program is using a USB drive when Windows refuses to eject it.'
  - autoEject: true
    $name: Eject automatically when the programs close
    $description: >-
      The initial state of the dialog's checkbox. When it's checked, the dialog
      stays open and ejects the drive as soon as all blocking programs have
      exited.
  - programButtons: true
    $name: Show Close and End buttons
    $description: >-
      Show a button for each blocking program. Programs with windows are asked to
      close, and background processes are ended.
  - elevatedEndTask: true
    $name: Allow closing programs that run as administrator
    $description: >-
      Show buttons with a UAC shield for blocking programs that run as
      administrator in your session.
  - forceEject: true
    $name: Show Force eject
    $description: >-
      Offer a last-resort button that flushes and dismounts the drive after a UAC
      prompt, and then ejects it. Programs may lose unsaved changes to files on
      the drive.
  - reportWaitMs: 1500
    $name: Wait for the list of programs (milliseconds)
    $description: >-
      How long to wait for Windows to report the blocking programs before the
      dialog opens. The list keeps updating while the dialog is open.
  $name: Better eject message
- doubleF2:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'F2 twice renames the ending: on'
    $description: 'Press F2 again to select just the file ending.'
  - DoubleF2MilliSeconds: 1000
    $name: Double F2 timing
    $description: >
      Time window for double press (milliseconds, 100-10000)
  - ContinuousLoop: false
    $name: Continuous loop
    $description: >
      Disable double F2 timing and just loop on every single F2 press. Selections
      that don't match one of the steps reset the cycle.
  - ReverseCycle: false
    $name: Swap double/triple F2
    $description: >
      Select the whole name on double F2 and the extension on triple F2?
  $name: F2 twice renames the ending
- noExtensionWarning:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'No rename warning: on'
    $description: 'Turns off the warning when you change a file ending.'
  $name: No rename warning
- harmfulFilesAccept:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'No harmful files question: on'
    $description: 'Skips the question ''These files might be harmful'' when you drag files.'
  $name: No harmful files question
- mediaKeyFix:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Play key goes to your player: on'
    $description: 'The play key reaches your music player instead of the selected file.'
  $name: Play key goes to your player
- treeGuard:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Folder tree crash guard: on'
    $description: 'Stops a File Explorer window from closing by itself when the folder tree gets a bad request.'
  $name: Folder tree crash guard
- previewDownloads:
  - enabled: true
    $name: 'Preview downloaded files: on'
    $description: 'The preview pane shows downloaded PDFs again. The file keeps its downloaded mark, so everything else stays as careful as before.'
  - extensions: pdf
    $name: Extensions
    $description: >-
      Comma-separated list of file extensions to preview even when the file is
      marked as downloaded from the Internet, without the dot. For example, pdf,
      txt, png. Executable, script, macro-enabled, archive and similar types are
      always ignored.
  - pathContains: ""
    $name: Only when the path contains
    $description: >-
      Optional. If not empty, only files whose path contains this text are
      exempted (not case sensitive). For example, \Downloads\
  $name: Preview downloaded files
*/
// ==/WindhawkModSettings==
// Seamless Explorer 1.1.2 is generated by gen.py from the live sources of 35 small Explorer mods.
// Each module keeps its own code in its own namespace, with its own saved-data folder; the dispatcher is last.
// ============================================================================
// Seamless Explorer: hook chaining.
// Windhawk refuses a second hook on a function one mod already hooked. Every module here lives
// in one mod, so each target gets one real hook, and the modules' hooks are called one after the
// other (first one registered is called first). Each module's "original function" pointer is a small
// stub that leads on to the next module's hook, and the last one leads to the real original.
// The module code itself is untouched: Wh_SetFunctionHook (and the typed wrappers in
// windhawk_utils.h) and HookSymbols are the only calls that go through this layer.
// ============================================================================
#ifndef NOMINMAX
#define NOMINMAX
#endif
#include <windows.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <wchar.h>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>

BOOL suite_HookRaw(void* target, void* hook, void** original);
#define Wh_SetFunctionHook(target, hook, original) suite_HookRaw((target), (hook), (original))

namespace suitehook {

constexpr int kMaxLinks = 12;
constexpr size_t kStubSize = 32;
constexpr size_t kSlabSize = 65536;

struct Chain {
    void* key;                  // the real function, jump thunks followed
    void* real;                 // what the last link continues to; Windhawk writes the trampoline here
    void* hook[kMaxLinks];      // the modules' hook functions, in call order
    uint8_t* stub[kMaxLinks];   // stub k is module k's "original function"
    int count;
    uint8_t* head;              // the stub Windhawk really hooks in; jumps to hook[0]
};

inline SRWLOCK g_lock = SRWLOCK_INIT;
inline std::vector<Chain*> g_chains;
inline std::vector<uint8_t*> g_slabs;
inline uint8_t* g_next = nullptr;
inline size_t g_left = 0;

inline bool Readable(const void* p, size_t n) {
    MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION mbi;
    if (!VirtualQuery(p, &mbi, sizeof(mbi))) return false;
    if (mbi.State != MEM_COMMIT || (mbi.Protect & (PAGE_NOACCESS | PAGE_GUARD))) return false;
    return (const uint8_t*)p + n <= (const uint8_t*)mbi.BaseAddress + mbi.RegionSize;
}

// Follows "jmp [rip+x]" (import stubs) and "jmp rel32" (incremental link tables) a few steps.
inline void* Resolve(void* p) {
    for (int hop = 0; hop < 4; hop++) {
        const uint8_t* b = (const uint8_t*)p;
        if (!Readable(b, 6)) break;
        if (b[0] == 0xFF && b[1] == 0x25) {
            const void* const* slot = (const void* const*)(b + 6 + *(const int32_t*)(b + 2));
            if (!Readable(slot, sizeof(void*)) || !*slot) break;
            p = (void*)*slot;
        } else if (b[0] == 0xE9) {
            p = (void*)(b + 5 + *(const int32_t*)(b + 1));
        } else {
            break;
        }
    }
    return p;
}

// A stub is: mov rax,[rip+9] ; jmp [rax] ; padding ; 8 byte slot at +16.
// The slot holds the address of a pointer variable, and the jump goes to whatever that variable holds.
inline uint8_t* NewStub(void** variable) {
    if (g_left < kStubSize) {
        uint8_t* slab = (uint8_t*)VirtualAlloc(nullptr, kSlabSize, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE);
        if (!slab) return nullptr;
        g_slabs.push_back(slab);
        g_next = slab;
        g_left = kSlabSize;
    }
    uint8_t* s = g_next;
    g_next += kStubSize;
    g_left -= kStubSize;
    static const uint8_t code[9] = {0x48, 0x8B, 0x05, 0x09, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0xFF, 0x20};
    memcpy(s, code, sizeof(code));
    memset(s + sizeof(code), 0xCC, 16 - sizeof(code));
    *(void***)(s + 16) = variable;
    memset(s + 24, 0xCC, 8);
    FlushInstructionCache(GetCurrentProcess(), s, kStubSize);
    return s;
}

inline void Retarget(uint8_t* stub, void** variable) {
    InterlockedExchangePointer((PVOID volatile*)(stub + 16), (PVOID)variable);
}

inline BOOL Register(void* target, void* hook, void** original) {
    if (!target || !hook) return (Wh_SetFunctionHook)(target, hook, original);
    void* key = Resolve(target);
    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
    Chain* c = nullptr;
    for (Chain* x : g_chains) {
        if (x->key == key) {
            c = x;
            break;
        }
    }
    bool fresh = false;
    if (!c) {
        c = new Chain{};
        c->key = key;
        c->real = key;
        c->head = NewStub(&c->hook[0]);
        if (!c->head) {
            delete c;
            ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
            return (Wh_SetFunctionHook)(target, hook, original);  // no executable memory: plain hook
        }
        fresh = true;
    } else {
        for (int i = 0; i < c->count; i++) {
            if (c->hook[i] == hook) {
                if (original) *original = c->stub[i];
                ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
                return TRUE;
            }
        }
        if (c->count == kMaxLinks) {
            ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
            return FALSE;
        }
    }
    uint8_t* link = NewStub(&c->real);
    if (!link) {
        if (fresh) delete c;
        ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
        return FALSE;
    }
    int k = c->count;
    c->hook[k] = hook;
    c->stub[k] = link;
    if (k > 0) Retarget(c->stub[k - 1], &c->hook[k]);
    c->count = k + 1;
    if (original) *original = link;
    BOOL ok = TRUE;
    if (fresh) {
        ok = (Wh_SetFunctionHook)(key, c->head, &c->real);
        if (ok) {
            g_chains.push_back(c);
        } else {
            delete c;
        }
    }
    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
    return ok;
}

// Called once when the mod unloads, after Windhawk has taken its hooks out.
inline void Shutdown() {
    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
    for (Chain* c : g_chains) delete c;
    g_chains.clear();
    for (uint8_t* s : g_slabs) VirtualFree(s, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
    g_slabs.clear();
    g_next = nullptr;
    g_left = 0;
    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
}

}  // namespace suitehook

BOOL suite_HookRaw(void* target, void* hook, void** original) {
    return suitehook::Register(target, hook, original);
}

#include <windhawk_utils.h>

namespace suitehook {

// WindhawkUtils::HookSymbols resolves the names and hooks each one itself. Here it only resolves
// them (hook left out), and the hooks go through Register, so two modules can hook one function.
struct SymbolHookView {  // the same layout as WindhawkUtils::SYMBOL_HOOK
    void* symbols;
    size_t symbolsCount;
    void** originalFunction;
    void* hookFunction;
    bool optional;
};
static_assert(sizeof(SymbolHookView) == sizeof(WindhawkUtils::SYMBOL_HOOK));

inline bool HookSymbols(HMODULE module, const WindhawkUtils::SYMBOL_HOOK* symbolHooks, size_t count,
                        const WH_HOOK_SYMBOLS_OPTIONS* options = nullptr) {
    const SymbolHookView* src = reinterpret_cast<const SymbolHookView*>(symbolHooks);
    std::vector<SymbolHookView> view(src, src + count);
    std::vector<void*> found(count, nullptr);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        if (view[i].hookFunction) {
            view[i].originalFunction = &found[i];
            view[i].hookFunction = nullptr;
        }
    }
    bool ok = WindhawkUtils::HookSymbols(
        module, reinterpret_cast<const WindhawkUtils::SYMBOL_HOOK*>(view.data()), count, options);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        if (src[i].hookFunction && found[i]) {
            void* ignored = nullptr;
            Register(found[i], src[i].hookFunction, src[i].originalFunction ? src[i].originalFunction : &ignored);
        }
    }
    return ok;
}

}  // namespace suitehook



// ============================================================================
// Seamless Explorer: setting names and setting watch.
// Every module reads its settings under its own name (tags.collapsed, copyQueue.speed and so on).
// Around each module a macro sends its Wh_GetIntSetting and Wh_GetStringSetting calls here, and
// the module's name is put in front of the setting name. A module that asks for a reload on every
// settings change (or has settings but cannot say what changed) also gets a watch slot: the
// values it read are kept, and it reloads only when one of them really changed.
// ============================================================================
#include <mutex>

namespace suitefp {

constexpr int kNone = -1;

struct Rec {
    bool isString;
    std::wstring value;
};
inline std::mutex g_mutex;
inline std::map<std::wstring, Rec> g_recs[2];

inline std::wstring Format(PCWSTR fmt, va_list args) {
    WCHAR buf[512];
    int n = _vsnwprintf(buf, 511, fmt, args);
    if (n < 0) n = 0;
    buf[n] = 0;
    return buf;
}

inline int GetIntV(int slot, PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR key, va_list a) {
    std::wstring full = std::wstring(prefix) + Format(key, a);
    int v = (Wh_GetIntSetting)(L"%s", full.c_str());
    if (slot >= 0) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_mutex);
        g_recs[slot][full] = Rec{false, std::to_wstring(v)};
    }
    return v;
}

inline PCWSTR GetStrV(int slot, PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR key, va_list a) {
    std::wstring full = std::wstring(prefix) + Format(key, a);
    PCWSTR v = (Wh_GetStringSetting)(L"%s", full.c_str());
    if (slot >= 0) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_mutex);
        g_recs[slot][full] = Rec{true, v ? v : L""};
    }
    return v;
}

inline int GetInt(int slot, PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR key, ...) {
    va_list a;
    va_start(a, key);
    int v = GetIntV(slot, prefix, key, a);
    va_end(a);
    return v;
}

inline PCWSTR GetStr(int slot, PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR key, ...) {
    va_list a;
    va_start(a, key);
    PCWSTR v = GetStrV(slot, prefix, key, a);
    va_end(a);
    return v;
}

// WindhawkUtils::StringSetting::make, with the module's name in front.
inline WindhawkUtils::StringSetting MakeStr(int slot, PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR key, ...) {
    va_list a;
    va_start(a, key);
    PCWSTR v = GetStrV(slot, prefix, key, a);
    va_end(a);
    return WindhawkUtils::StringSetting(v);
}

// True when any watched setting differs from what the module read last.
inline bool Changed(int slot) {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_mutex);
    if (g_recs[slot].empty()) return true;  // nothing watched: trust the module
    bool changed = false;
    for (auto& kv : g_recs[slot]) {
        std::wstring now;
        if (kv.second.isString) {
            PCWSTR v = (Wh_GetStringSetting)(L"%s", kv.first.c_str());
            now = v ? v : L"";
            if (v) Wh_FreeStringSetting(v);
        } else {
            now = std::to_wstring((Wh_GetIntSetting)(L"%s", kv.first.c_str()));
        }
        if (now != kv.second.value) {
            changed = true;
            kv.second.value = now;
        }
    }
    return changed;
}

}  // namespace suitefp


// ============================================================================
// Seamless Explorer: saved data, one share per module.
// All modules here are one Windhawk mod, so they would share one set of saved values and one storage
// folder. Around each module that saves anything, a macro sends its Wh_GetIntValue, Wh_SetIntValue,
// Wh_GetStringValue, Wh_SetStringValue, Wh_GetBinaryValue, Wh_SetBinaryValue, Wh_DeleteValue and
// Wh_GetModStoragePath calls here. Saved value names get the module name in front (tags.collapsed), and
// the storage folder becomes "<mod storage>\<module>", made on first use.
// ============================================================================
namespace suitestore {

inline std::wstring Name(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name) {
    return std::wstring(prefix) + (name ? name : L"");
}

inline int GetInt(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, int def) {
    return (Wh_GetIntValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), def);
}

inline BOOL SetInt(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, int value) {
    return (Wh_SetIntValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), value);
}

inline size_t GetStr(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, PWSTR buffer, size_t chars) {
    return (Wh_GetStringValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), buffer, chars);
}

inline BOOL SetStr(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, PCWSTR value) {
    return (Wh_SetStringValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), value);
}

inline size_t GetBin(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, void* buffer, size_t bytes) {
    return (Wh_GetBinaryValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), buffer, bytes);
}

inline BOOL SetBin(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name, const void* buffer, size_t bytes) {
    return (Wh_SetBinaryValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str(), buffer, bytes);
}

inline BOOL Delete(PCWSTR prefix, PCWSTR name) {
    return (Wh_DeleteValue)(Name(prefix, name).c_str());
}

// Same answer as Wh_GetModStoragePath: the length without the end mark, or 0 when the buffer is too small.
inline size_t Path(PCWSTR module, PWSTR buffer, size_t chars) {
    WCHAR base[MAX_PATH * 2];
    size_t n = (Wh_GetModStoragePath)(base, ARRAYSIZE(base));
    if (!n || n >= ARRAYSIZE(base)) return 0;
    std::wstring dir = std::wstring(base) + L"\\" + module;
    if (dir.size() + 1 > chars) return 0;
    CreateDirectoryW(base, nullptr);  // normally there already
    if (!CreateDirectoryW(dir.c_str(), nullptr) && GetLastError() != ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS) return 0;
    wmemcpy(buffer, dir.c_str(), dir.size() + 1);
    return dir.size();
}

}  // namespace suitestore

